Rankings and MP/funder summaries need a consistent registration-period filter. History needs the full archive with its existing date controls.

## What changed

- Apply backend registration windows before detail aggregation, recipient limits and ranking top tens.
- Share period controls across rankings and entity summaries, preserve scroll during filter loads, and keep history independent of the Summary period.
- Split the Latest declarations category wheel horizontally, with MPs above Companies. Full-width native hit targets keep labels upright and preserve the existing rankings quadrants.

## Scope

- Historical includes all records and undated declarations. The term starts inclusively at 2024-07-09T00:00:00Z. This year is the full UTC calendar year.
- Preserve all categories for member totals and the existing donation/support scope for other ranking boards. Preserve exact decimals, currencies, declaration and funding-entry counts, null versus zero, and completeness rules.
- Default rankings and summaries to the current term. The backend returns all three complete headline totals. History loads all stored declarations and retains its date filters, pagination and Summary return context.

## Blast radius

Updates the rankings and entity API/SSR contracts together. Entity identity and latest party attribution remain unchanged. The shared category wheel accepts explicit sector bounds; existing ranking quadrants retain their default dimensions.

## Verification

- Passed 196 frontend tests, frontend check/build and commit-hook clippy. Backend coverage includes 139 passing Rust tests and focused current-term checks. Independent reviews found no actionable issues.
- Real preview checks cover preserved scroll, complete history, and horizontal wheel pointer/keyboard behavior on desktop and mobile.
- Snapshot comparison retains the same pre-existing BBC, GB News and Premier League differences. Those differences reproduce on main; full production parity is not claimed.${images}`;
